  "id": "DrugBank_DB07615 - MONDO_grouped_11786_5324_24332",
  "verbalization": "Tranilast, a drug primarily used for its anti-inflammatory properties, is implicated in the pathogenesis of Allergic Rhinitis through a series of mechanistic links. The evidence suggests that Tranilast may exert a modulatory effect on Vasomotor Rhinitis, which is a common form of allergic rhinitis characterized by nasal vasodilation and hyperactivity. This effect is further mediated by the drug's interaction with other agents such as Mebhydrolin and Mizolastine, which also show indications of contributing to Allergic Rhinitis. The shared pathway from Tranilast to Vasomotor Rhinitis and then to Allergic Rhinitis implies a potential mechanism involving the modulation of inflammatory responses or mast cell activation. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Allergic Rhinitis suggests a possible role for Tranilast in the treatment of this condition, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Tranilast may have a therapeutic role in Allergic Rhinitis, though further research is needed to confirm its efficacy and safety profile.",
